---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import warm from '../assets/warm.jpg';
import ExperimentOverview from './ExperimentOverview.astro';
import meter from '../assets/meter.jpg';
import poster from '../assets/video-poster.jpg';
const conditions=[
 {id:'B',light:'warm',tempo:'slow',bpm:68,date:'Tuesday, 18 August',n:25},
 {id:'A',light:'warm',tempo:'fast',bpm:118,date:'Wednesday, 19 August',n:37},
 {id:'D',light:'cool',tempo:'slow',bpm:68,date:'Thursday, 20 August',n:30},
 {id:'C',light:'cool',tempo:'fast',bpm:118,date:'Friday, 21 August',n:36},
];
---
<section id="experiment" class="experiment wrap" aria-labelledby="experiment-heading">
 <div class="section-line light-line"><span>The experiment</span><span>Soundscape × lighting</span></div>
 <div class="experiment-grid"><div><h2 id="experiment-heading">A different tempo.<br />A different light.<br />The same space.</h2><p>How do sound and light shape the way we experience a store? This exploratory UCL study brings the two together in a real retail environment.</p><p>Each musical tempo is paired with warm and cool lighting, creating four conditions. The study explores comfort, mood, movement and time spent in the space.</p></div>
 <ExperimentOverview /></div>
 <div class="conditions-scene">
  <Image class="conditions-backdrop" src={warm} alt="" widths={[800,1400,2000]} sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw, 92vw" width={2000} height={1333} loading="lazy" />
  <div class="conditions-scene-content">
   <div class="conditions-heading"><p>UCL Store experiment</p><h3>Explore the experimental conditions</h3><p>Select a condition to hear the combination of lighting and music used in the study.</p></div>
   <div class="experiment-gallery">{conditions.map(c=><button class="experiment-card" data-combination={c.bpm} data-light={c.light} data-condition={c.id} aria-pressed="false" aria-label={`Play 30-second excerpt: ${c.light} light + ${c.bpm} BPM`}>
    <span class="condition-card-label">Condition {c.id}</span>
    <strong>{c.light === 'warm'?'Warm':'Cool'} + {c.tempo}</strong>
    <span class="condition-card-meta"><span>{c.bpm} BPM</span><span>n = {c.n}</span></span>
    <span class="sample-action" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sample-icon"><svg class="sample-play" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="16" height="16"><path d="M5 3v14l12-7Z" fill="currentColor" /></svg><svg class="sample-stop" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="16" height="16"><path d="M4 4h12v12H4Z" fill="currentColor" /></svg></span><span class="sample-text">Listen · 30 sec</span></span>
    <span class="sample-progress" aria-hidden="true"></span>
   </button>)}</div>
   <div class="condition-scene-footer"><div class="sample-transport"><p id="matrix-status" role="status">Choose a condition to listen. The excerpt uses the same player above.</p><button id="sample-stop" hidden>Stop excerpt</button></div><span>Sound / light / people / space</span></div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <p class="matrix-note">Photographs document the lighting conditions. Screen colour does not reproduce calibrated lighting.</p>
</section>
<section class="place wrap" aria-labelledby="place-heading">
 <div class="place-caption"><p class="eyebrow">The setting</p><h2 id="place-heading">One space.<br />A changing light.</h2><p>Watch the store move between neutral, warm and cool light. The silent film keeps the focus on colour temperature while you listen.</p></div>
 <figure class="lighting-film"><div class="film-stage"><video id="lighting-video" muted playsinline loop controls preload="none" poster={poster.src} width="1024" height="576" aria-label="Silent video of lighting changes in the UCL Store"><source src="/video/lighting.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/video/lighting.vtt" srclang="en" label="Lighting conditions" /><p>Your browser cannot play the video. <a href="/video/lighting.mp4">Open the silent film</a>.</p></video><div class="film-label" data-light="neutral"><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span id="video-light-label">Neutral light</span></div></div><figcaption><span>Light in transition · The Hanger, UCL Store</span><span>Silent film · 0:54</span></figcaption></figure>
 <p id="video-status" class="video-status" role="status">The film plays silently when in view. Use the video controls to pause or seek.</p>
</section>
<section id="methodology" class="methodology wrap" aria-labelledby="method-heading"><div class="section-line light-line"><span>Research notes</span><span>UCL / IEDE / 2026</span></div><div class="method-grid"><div class="method-intro"><h2 id="method-heading">Listening is <br />the starting point.</h2><figure class="measurement-photo"><Image src={meter} alt="A lux meter and sound level meter used to document the store environment" widths={[400,700]} sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw, 35vw" width={700} height={933} loading="lazy" /><figcaption>In the field: documenting illuminance and sound level alongside the listening conditions.</figcaption></figure></div><div><details open><summary>Study methodology <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A mixed-methods pilot combining direct observation, short customer surveys, staff feedback and environmental measurements. The factorial design crosses music tempo with lighting colour temperature.</p><p>Observation focuses on dwell time and movement. Questionnaires explore perceived comfort, mood, engagement and spatial experience. Sound pressure and illuminance are measured in the store.</p><p>The overview reports respondent counts for each condition. This page presents the stimuli and study setting, not findings about their effects. Descriptions of musical mood refer to the intended character of the recordings.</p></details><details id="analysis-method"><summary>How to read the audio <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Waveform: RMS amplitude of a mono downmix in 5-second windows. Spectrogram and file-average frequency profile: Hann-window FFT (2,048 samples), analysed at 24 kHz, displayed from 30 Hz to 12 kHz. File average shows mean spectral power across the whole recording. Both recordings share the same plotting scales.</p><p>Loudness: EBU R128 analysis of the supplied X3 stereo files. Integrated loudness is shown in LUFS, loudness range in LU and true peak in dBTP. The loudness curve shows 3-second short-term readings averaged in 5-second windows.</p><p>The recordings are played at their original speed, without loudness normalisation. The BPM labels identify the supplied conditions; they are not an automatic tempo estimate. Digital loudness does not measure the store’s sound pressure level.</p><p>Live spectrum uses Web Audio FFT with a Blackman window, at the browser’s audio sample rate, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz (or Nyquist). Resolution selects the FFT size; Response controls smoothing. The display updates about 30 times per second during playback, less often with reduced motion. Peak hold decays at 8 dB per second. Freeze holds the visual while audio continues. The analyser sits before playback volume. Live and file-average spectra use different windows and aggregation, so their values are not directly interchangeable.</p><p>File visualisations use <a href="https://d3js.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D3</a>. The playhead follows the audio position. The spectrogram uses a shared black–violet–red–yellow scale.</p></details><details><summary>Research & credits <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p><strong>Module</strong><br />BENV0008 25/26</p><p><strong>Supervisors</strong><br />Dr Francesco Aletta<br />Dr Gemma Moore</p><p>MSc Health, Wellbeing and Sustainable Buildings<br />UCL Institute for Environmental Design and Engineering</p><p>Research title: “The Influence of Soundscape and Lighting on Customer Behaviour and Spatial Experience in Retail Environments”.</p><p>Audio: the supplied <em>bruna-tracks68bpmX3</em> and <em>bruna-118bpmX3</em> recordings. Research context: June and August 2026 project presentations. Photographs, experiment overview and lighting video supplied by the project.</p></details></div></div></section>
<footer class="footer wrap"><a class="footer-title" href="#listen">Return to listening <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div><span>BENV0008 25/26</span><span>UCL · MSc dissertation · 2026</span><a href="#">Back to top ↑</a></div></footer>

<script>import '../scripts/experiment.ts';</script>
